# ──────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# Allowlist strategy: ignore everything at the repo ROOT by default,
# then explicitly re-include the source / documentation trees.
#
# `/*` is ANCHORED to the repo root, so it only ignores top-level
# entries (data/, ecg_env/, processed/, stray files, …) and does NOT
# re-ignore files nested inside the folders we re-include below.
#
# data/  and  ecg_env/  are never re-included → they can never be
# committed (raw + processed datasets stay local only).
# ──────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
/*

# --- allow project source & documentation (whole subtrees) ---
!/.gitignore
!/.gitattributes
!/AGENTS.md
!/CLAUDE.md
!/phase_1_summary_report.md
!/config/
!/docs/
!/scripts/
!/paper/
!/report_assets/

# --- outputs: ignore the whole tree, then allow ONLY text reports
#     & result tables. figures/ and model_runs/ (.png/.pt) and the
#     root .docx stay out. ---
!/outputs/
/outputs/*
!/outputs/audit_reports/
!/outputs/stage_reports/
!/outputs/tables/

# --- never commit logs, caches, or notebook checkpoints anywhere ---
**/logs/
*.log
**/__pycache__/
*.py[cod]
.ipynb_checkpoints/

# --- hard safety net: dataset / binary blobs must NEVER be committed,
#     even if one ever lands inside an allowed folder by mistake.
#     (Intentionally excludes *.png/*.jpg/*.pdf/*.csv so paper figures,
#      report-asset images, and small result CSVs stay tracked.) ---
*.csv.gz
*.gz
*.h5
*.hdf5
*.npy
*.dat
*.hea
*.parquet
*.pt
*.pth
*.ckpt
